      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:gs"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-gs-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-gs-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 7 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Fuel seasons by billing month. FCR-27 prices June through September and October through May, which Schedule R's bills show is read by the billing month a bill is rendered in. The JSON-LD gates the fuel PriceDefinitions on calendar months, so usage in the weeks a billing period runs ahead of its billing month takes the other season's fuel price. (2) Voltage level and franchise fee location. FCR-27's three voltage levels and MFF-11's two locations are crossed in one ProfileAlternatives set of six alternatives, because URPX v0.5.1 allows one set per PlanElements and the franchise fee's energy subtotal must include that voltage level's fuel prices. A consumer selects one alternative, for example Secondary Distribution inside city limits. (3) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the non-energy charges' Prices, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (4) Demand Side Management schedule. The sheet applies \"the Company's effective Demand Side Management Residential or Commercial Schedule\". DSM-C-15 applies to all Commercial Customers as the Company's Rules and Regulations for Electric Service define them, and is carried here as Prices with no condition, so it applies to every customer on the schedule. A Residential Customer served on the schedule would pay DSM-R-16, 1.1969 percent, instead; the sheet names no schedule for an Industrial Customer. Neither case is carried. (5) Minimum Monthly Bill. The sheet sets it at the $36.00 Basic Service Charge plus ECCR, DSM, Fuel Cost Recovery on the current month's kWh and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every price here is zero or positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it. (6) General Service - Unmetered (GS-U). Where the Company finds metering impractical or uneconomical, monthly kWh may be estimated and billed at this rate, for customers continuously served on the unmetered option since December 31, 2019. Estimating the kWh is not carried; the prices apply to whatever kWh a consumer supplies. (7) Construction Service and Term of Contract. Construction power is part of permanent service, with a payment in advance per metering point in the amount on file with the Commission; the term is one year unless the customer elects to return to the FlatBill-GS tariff. Neither is priced on the sheet and neither is carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
